# oracle: bond_style bpm/spring volume/factor yes (native: b332f28 as the installed lmp, BPM package), cut down from
# examples/bpm/poissons_ratio/in.bpm.poissons_ratio: a 2 x 2 x 2 cube of 8 atoms with all 12 nearest-neighbour bonds, the
# top layer pushed down and the bottom layer up (a squeeze), bond_coeff 1 1.0 0.1 1.0 -0.8 (k, epsilon_c, gamma, av) with
# break yes and smooth yes, so bonds break and the reference volumes change (vol0 update) in the 200 steps.
# measured: max relative error 1.0e-14 over the thermo rows and the per-atom state (native b332f28 = installed lmp, BPM package)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units lj
dimension 3
boundary f f f
atom_style bond
newton on off
comm_modify vel yes cutoff 2.6
lattice sc 1.0
region box block -1 3 -1 3 -1 3 units box
create_box 1 box bond/types 1 extra/bond/per/atom 6
region cube block 0 1 0 1 0 1 units box
create_atoms 1 region cube
mass 1 1.0
pair_style bpm/spring
pair_coeff 1 1 1.0 1.0 1.0
create_bonds many all all 1 0.0 1.1
region top block -1 3 -1 3 0.6 3 units box
region bot block -1 3 -1 3 -1 0.4 units box
group top region top
group bot region bot
velocity top set 0.0 0.0 -0.3
velocity bot set 0.0 0.0 0.3
neighbor 0.3 bin
special_bonds lj 0.0 1.0 1.0 coul 1.0 1.0 1.0
bond_style bpm/spring volume/factor yes
bond_coeff 1 1.0 0.1 1.0 -0.8
fix 1 all nve
compute nb all nbond/atom
compute tb all reduce sum c_nb
thermo_style custom step ke pe ebond c_tb
thermo_modify format float %.15g norm no lost ignore lost/bond ignore
timestep 0.01
thermo 40
run 200
